**The oh-my-auggie repository at `github.com/r3dlex/oh-my-auggie` is private and could not be accessed externally.** This specification therefore documents every oh-my-claudecode (OMC) component that must exist in oh-my-auggie (OMA), mapped precisely to Auggie CLI's plugin architecture. Where the user's prompt names existing OMA files (v0.1.4, 64 commits), this spec treats those as the baseline and identifies every gap against OMC v4.11.x. The Auggie plugin system is **fully compatible** with the Claude Code plugin format — `.augment-plugin/` works identically to `.claude-plugin/`, and hooks, commands, agents, rules, skills, and MCP servers follow the same directory conventions.

---

## The oh-my-auggie repo is private — what this changes

Because the repository could not be fetched, the 15 filesystem questions (items 1–15 in the task) cannot be answered with verified file contents. Every directory listing, config file, and source excerpt below is **inferred from the user's description** of v0.1.4 (plugins/oma/ with agents/, commands/, hooks/, rules/, skills/, mcp/ subdirectories; a state-server.mjs MCP server; a CLI in cli/; executables in bin/; e2e tests; scripts/; adr/ for ADRs; SPEC.md, CHANGELOG.md, prd.json; .augment-plugin manifests; .mcp.json). The delta spec assumes these exist as described and focuses on what OMC has that OMA likely does not yet.

