## 4. The 7 missing keyword triggers

OMC's `keyword-detector.mjs` fires on the **UserPromptSubmit** event. It sanitizes user input (strips code blocks), then pattern-matches magic keywords that activate skills. The 7 likely missing triggers:

| # | Keyword(s) | Activates | Behavior |
|---|-----------|----------|----------|
| 1 | `autopilot`, `auto pilot` | autopilot skill | Sets autopilot-state.json, injects full SKILL.md into context |
| 2 | `ralph`, `don't stop`, `must complete` | ralph skill | Sets ralph-state.json with iteration counter |
| 3 | `ulw`, `ultrawork` | ultrawork skill | Sets ultrawork-state.json, enables parallel delegation |
| 4 | `ralplan` | ralplan skill | Activates consensus planning loop |
| 5 | `ultraqa` | ultraqa skill | Starts automated QA cycling |
| 6 | `team N:agent` | team skill | Parses N (worker count) and agent type, launches coordinated workers |
| 7 | `stopomc` / `cancel` / `abort` | cancel skill | Reads active state files, clears them, injects cancellation confirmation |

### File to create: `plugins/oma/hooks/keyword-detector.mjs`

```javascript
#!/usr/bin/env node
import { readFileSync, writeFileSync, existsSync, mkdirSync } from 'fs';
import { join } from 'path';

const input = JSON.parse(readFileSync('/dev/stdin', 'utf8'));
const prompt = (input.tool_input?.prompt || input.tool_input?.message || '').toString();
const conversationId = input.conversation_id || 'default';
const projectDir = process.env.AUGMENT_PROJECT_DIR || '.';
const pluginRoot = process.env.AUGMENT_PLUGIN_ROOT || '.';
const stateDir = join(projectDir, '.oma', 'state', 'sessions', conversationId);

// Sanitize: strip code blocks before matching
const sanitized = prompt.replace(/```[\s\S]*?```/g, '').toLowerCase().trim();

const KEYWORDS = [
  { pattern: /\bautopilot\b|auto pilot/, skill: 'autopilot', mode: 'autopilot' },
  { pattern: /\bralph\b|don'?t stop|must complete|keep going/, skill: 'ralph', mode: 'ralph' },
  { pattern: /\bulw\b|\bultrawork\b/, skill: 'ultrawork', mode: 'ultrawork' },
  { pattern: /\bralplan\b/, skill: 'ralplan', mode: 'ralplan' },
  { pattern: /\bultraqa\b/, skill: 'ultraqa', mode: 'ultraqa' },
  { pattern: /\bteam\s+(\d+):(\w+)/, skill: 'team', mode: 'team' },
  { pattern: /\bstopomc\b|\bcancel\b|\babort\b/, skill: 'cancel', mode: null },
];

const result = { hookSpecificOutput: { hookEventName: 'UserPromptSubmit' } };

for (const kw of KEYWORDS) {
  const match = sanitized.match(kw.pattern);
  if (match) {
    // Load skill content and inject as additionalContext
    const skillPath = join(pluginRoot, 'plugins', 'oma', 'skills', kw.skill, 'SKILL.md');
    let skillContent = '';
    if (existsSync(skillPath)) {
      skillContent = readFileSync(skillPath, 'utf8');
    }

    // Write mode state if activating a mode
    if (kw.mode) {
      if (!existsSync(stateDir)) mkdirSync(stateDir, { recursive: true });
      writeFileSync(join(stateDir, `${kw.mode}-state.json`), JSON.stringify({
        active: true, mode: kw.mode, iteration: 1, maxIterations: 50,
        session_id: conversationId, started: new Date().toISOString()
      }, null, 2));
    }

    result.hookSpecificOutput.additionalContext =
      `[OMA] Activated ${kw.skill} mode via keyword "${match[0]}".\n\n${skillContent}`;
    break;
  }
}

process.stdout.write(JSON.stringify(result));
```

