## Conclusion

The delta from OMA v0.1.4 to OMC feature parity spans **63 new files** across 6 tiers: 6 hook scripts, 9 MCP tool additions to state-server.mjs, 16 command definitions, 15 agent definitions, 13 skill definitions, and several rule/documentation updates. The single most impactful addition is the **PostToolUse hook with `additionalContext` injection** — this creates the feedback loop that makes persistent modes, subagent tracking, and live status possible. Without it, ralph/autopilot/ultrawork modes cannot function because the agent has no way to receive orchestration state between tool calls.

The second most impactful addition is the **keyword-detector on UserPromptSubmit** — this delivers OMC's "zero learning curve" promise by letting users type natural language keywords instead of memorizing slash commands. Combined with the stop-continuation hook (which blocks premature termination during persistent modes), these three hooks form the **irreducible core** of the orchestration system. Everything else — agents, skills, commands, MCP tools — is content that these hooks orchestrate.

**Recommended implementation order:** PostToolUse hook → keyword-detector + stop-continuation → MCP notepad/skill/intent tools → ultrawork skill + executor/architect agents → ralph skill + critic/verifier agents → autopilot skill + remaining agents → remaining commands and skills. Each tier is independently testable and delivers incremental value.""
